      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2017 Wiley-VCH Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA, Weinheim.",
        "AbstractText": "Methanol (CH3 OH) and formaldehyde (H2 CO) molecules were inserted into an open-cage C60 derivative with a large opening, under high-pressure and high-temperature conditions in solution. Isolation of their molecular complexes in pure form was achieved by the use of recycling HPLC with Buckyprep columns. 1 H\u2005NMR spectroscopy, single-crystal X-ray diffraction studies, and DFT calculations revealed the orientation of the encapsulated CH3 OH and H2 CO, both in solution and in the solid state, and the results show that the CH3 group of the CH3 OH and the carbonyl group of the H2 CO point to the bottom of the cages. Furthermore, the dynamic behavior of the CH3 OH and H2 CO were studied at the molecular level."
      },
